 "capsule": "The state of Qi (齊) was a major Zhou fief on the Shandong Peninsula, traditionally founded around 1046 BCE when King Wu of Zhou enfeoffed the strategist Jiang Ziya (Duke Tai), with its long-lived capital at Linzi. Duke Huan (r. 685–643 BCE) made Qi the first hegemon of the Spring and Autumn period with the aid of his minister Guan Zhong, and in 386 BCE the ducal throne passed from the Jiang lineage to the Tian (Chen) clan, who ruled Qi as one of the seven major Warring States. Qi was the last independent state absorbed by Qin's unification wars, falling in 221 BCE.",
